From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Market Canopy <office@marketcanopy.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Market Canopy as the AI agent's only provider; no run_script
 or stdio MCP

ADR 0525: one managed provider, "marketcanopy", serves the AI agent. Its
code is in the overlay (src/providers/marketcanopy); this change wires it
in. The registry offers only that provider and resolves any stored
provider type to it, so a thread saved by an upstream build never uses
its stored key. main.tsx imports the bootstrap, which rewrites the stored
settings before the stores load, and the watcher, which cancels requests
in flight and reloads the models when the account or organization
changes. The settings page shows the Market Canopy connection instead of
the provider form; the Wallet description shows only when the Wallet is
shown. Saved MCP settings keep only URL servers.

Native code no longer runs processes for the agent: run_script is not
registered, and the renderer's _createProcess, which started stdio MCP
servers, refuses every call. file_opener's description stops pointing at
run_script.

A plugin in the user folder with the GUID of a bundled AI plugin (the
agent or the in-editor AI plugin) and a higher version no longer
replaces the bundled one, so a plugin from the store cannot bring back
the third-party providers.
